---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AgentSelector from '../components/AgentSelector.astro';
import InstallServer from '../components/InstallServer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Download & Setup | Blood Kings Monitoring" description="Install Blood Kings Monitoring on PHP hosting with MySQL and a cron job, then add agents for Linux, OpenWrt routers, Windows and Docker.">
  <section class="page-header section">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <span class="badge badge-accent">Download Center</span>
      <h1>Deploy Blood Kings Monitoring</h1>
      <p class="section-subtitle">Install the central server on your PHP hosting, then add lightweight agents to the machines and routers you want to watch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Server Deployment Panel; every "Install" CTA lands on #server. -->
  <section class="section bg-dim" id="server">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="download-section-header">
        <h2>1. Install the server</h2>
        <p>The server runs the checks, collects what the agents send, sends the alerts and serves the status pages. It is plain PHP with a MySQL database: no image to pull and nothing to build on the hosting.</p>
      </div>

      <InstallServer lang="en" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Agent Deployment Section; the server guide's last step links #agents. -->
  <section class="section" id="agents">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="download-section-header">
        <h2>2. Agents on your machines and routers</h2>
        <p>To see what happens inside a machine (CPU, memory, disks, network) or on a router (Wi-Fi, WAN, connected clients), install an agent on it.</p>
      </div>
      <AgentSelector lang="en" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GitHub Source Code CTA -->
  <section class="section bg-dim">
    <div class="container text-center github-cta-card">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Want to contribute?</h2>
        <p>The Blood Kings Monitoring system is 100% open-source, licensed under the MIT License. Contributions, documentation guides, and issue reports are welcome on GitHub.</p>
        <div class="github-links-row">
          <a href="https://github.com/BKPepe/monitoring" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">
            💻 GitHub Repository
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/BKPepe/monitoring/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-secondary">
            📦 Explore GitHub Releases
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 100%, var(--surface-1) 0%, transparent 60%);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .download-section-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .download-section-header h2 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .download-section-header p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-mid);
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
  }

  .github-cta-card {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .github-cta-card h2 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .github-cta-card p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0.5rem auto 2rem;
  }

  .github-links-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-header h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
